    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "it's just... everything feels so heavy. like the effort of living is just constant friction against the inevitable. if you're saying it's a \"decisive act\" to just stop, then it feels less like giving up and more like just being rational about how things work. it's like, why keep the engine running when we know the fuel is gone and the road ends in a cliff?",
